Tyler,

There is no Shiny Server for Windows at this time; the software is currently only compatible with Linux (although some brave souls have gotten it working on Mac as well). In the future we may offer a native Windows version of Shiny Server.

We also have a new Shiny hosting service in beta that will replace Glimmer and Spark (which can't easily be upgraded to R 3.0.2 without breaking existing users' code), that service is called ShinyApps <http://shinyapps.io> and is already on the latest version of R. It has a very different architecture from Glimmer/Spark that will prevent some of the problems that we have had with those servers.

