> Related to the common UI elements question I am wondering how you would deal with common output elements. For example, a set of (sub)-menu items that each have the same output elements (e.g., a Summary and a Plots) tab. It seems I would have to specify a tabsetPanel for each 'tool' as below.
>
> output$tabs_singleMean <- renderUI({
>   tabsetPanel(id = "singleMean",
>    tabPanel("Summary", verbatimTextOutput("summary.singleMean")),
>         tabPanel("Plots", plotOutput("plots.singleMean", height = "100%"))
>   )
> })

You could write a function that returns a tabsetPanel parameterized as desired. For example:

statPanel <- function(stat) {
  tabsetPanel(
    id = stat,
    tabPanel("Summary", verbatimTextOutput(paste0("summary.", stat))),
    tabPanel("Plots", plotOutput(paste0("plots.", stat), height = "100%"))
  )
}

